      "current": "Pages and SemanticStyles consume application-owned semantic Brush keys through ThemeResources.xaml and matching Palette.Light.xaml/Palette.Dark.xaml dictionaries; Wpf.Ui color names remain behind the control/theme provider boundary.",
      "sources": ["src/NovelSpeaker.App/Bootstrap/App.xaml", "src/NovelSpeaker.App/Shared/Theming/Resources/SemanticStyles.xaml", "src/NovelSpeaker.App/Shell/MainWindow.xaml", "src/NovelSpeaker.App/Features/Playback/Components/PlayerView.xaml"],
      "migrationTarget": "Create app-owned Palette.Light.xaml, Palette.Dark.xaml and ThemeResources.xaml. Map all page/control color use to AppBackground, CanvasSurface, PrimarySurface, SecondarySurface, RaisedSurface, text, border, Accent, state and focus semantic keys. Keep Wpf.Ui as the platform theme provider behind the mapping, not as a page-facing contract."
    },
    {
